PicoGKRuntime 26.2 (0f26321c) — ABI hardening: checked indices, bounded string
copies and an empty scalar field from voxels. Upstreamable to
leap71/PicoGKRuntime; not yet offered.

Applied to vendor/PicoGKRuntime by scripts/fetch-deps.sh after 0001-0006.
Kept as a patch because it modifies dependency source; no flag-level override
exists. Ledger rows U28 and U29 (upstream/LEDGER.md).

1. Source/PicoGKMesh.h, Source/PicoGKPolyLine.h, Source/PicoGKVdbFile.h —
   MI10/RC7: indices are checked in every build. Mesh::nAddTriangle throws
   std::out_of_range before any bookkeeping when a corner is not a vertex
   index (an assert compiled out of release builds stored the dangling
   index, and every later reader went out of bounds); GetVertex,
   GetTriangle, PolyLine::GetVertex and VdbFile::roGridAt read through
   vector::at, which throws for negative indices too. In this wasm build the
   asserts were live and aborted the module; a throw is a recoverable
   WebAssembly.Exception the facade maps to PicoError.
2. Source/PicoGKLibrary.cpp — RC5: Metadata_bGetNameAt and
   Metadata_bGetStringAt refuse a null or zero-length buffer, which
   strncpy(…, size_t(-1)) would write before. MI8/RC6 (Windows only):
   strncpy_s with _TRUNCATE instead of a count that aborts at 254 characters.
3. Source/PicoGKLibrary.cpp — RC4: ScalarField_hBuildFromVoxels starts from
   an empty field at the source's voxel size, as VectorField_hBuildFromVoxels
   does. Before, it started from a copy of the voxels, so every voxel the
   threshold did not select kept its signed distance.

Not included: MI5 (VdbFile_hGet* hand out the file's own grid, so reads alias
each other). Deep-copying the reads breaks the save path: C#'s
OpenVdbFile.SaveToFile and picovoxel's stampPicoMetadata write
PicoGK.VoxelSize and the library name through a read handle, and on a copy
those stamps never reach the file. A fix needs a metadata setter on the file
first.

Output: items 1 and 2 change only calls that were undefined behaviour or
aborted. Item 3 changes results wherever the field held stale distances.
picovoxel's byte-locked pins hold unchanged.
